hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20976","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Abu al-Malih from his father that the day of Hunayn was rainy. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered his caller that prayer is in the dwellings."
"20977","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it alike."
"20978","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us from Abu al-Malih from his father that they were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Hunayn, and rain befell them, so his caller called: Pray in your dwellings."
"20979","Bahz narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Abu al-Malih narrated to us from his father that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Hunayn on a rainy day: Prayer is in the dwellings."
"20980","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Malih who said: I prayed the last evening prayer in Basrah, and we were rained upon, then I came to open. Abu Usamah said to me: You saw us with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the time of Hudaybiyyah, we were rained upon and the sky did not wet the soles of our sandals, so the caller of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called: Pray in your dwellings."
"20981","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Khalid from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Malih from his father who said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Hudaybiyyah, and rain befell us not wetting the soles of our sandals, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray in your dwellings."
"20982","Ismail narrated to us, Said informed us, and Ibn Jafar, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah from his father that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the skins of predators."
"20983","Ismail narrated to us, Khalid informed us from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah who said: I went out to the mosque on a rainy night, and when I returned I knocked. My father said: Who is this. They said: Abu al-Malih. He said: You saw us with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the time of Hudaybiyyah, and a sky befell us not wetting the soles of our sandals, so the caller of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called: Pray in your dwellings."
"20984","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, Shubah narrated to me from Qatadah who said: I heard Abu al-Malih narrating from his father that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a house saying: Allah, mighty and majestic, does not accept prayer without purification nor charity from misappropriation."
"20985","Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Suhaymi narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Malih from his father that a man of his people freed a share of his of a slave, so that was raised to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he made his release upon him in his wealth and said: Allah, blessed and exalted, has no partner."
"20986","Bahz narrated to us from Hammam who said: The hadith of the share in the slave is mursal."
"20987","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us that Abu al-Malih informed him from his father that the day of Hunayn was a rainy day, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered his caller to call: Prayer is in the dwellings."
"20988","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Malih from his father that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the skins of predators."
"20989","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us from Abu al-Malih from his father that rain befell them at Hunayn, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray in the dwellings."
"20990","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Said, Qatadah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Malih narrating from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, mighty and majestic, does not accept charity from misappropriation nor prayer without purification."
"20991","Muhammad, and he is Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Malih from his father that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Hunayn on a rainy day ordering his caller, so he calls: Prayer is in the dwellings."
"20992","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Malih from his father that a man from Hudhayl freed a share of his of a slave, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He is free, all of him. Allah, blessed and exalted, has no partner."
"20993","Abu Said narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the like of it, and he did not mention from his father."
"20994","Surayj narrated to us, Abbad, meaning Ibn al-Awwam, narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah from his father that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Circumcision is a sunnah for men, honorable for women."
"20995","Yunus narrated to us, Aban narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Malih from his father that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered his caller on the day of Hunayn on a rainy day, so he called: Prayer is in the dwellings."
